<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:common="using:Telegram.Common"
                    xmlns:controls="using:Telegram.Controls"
                    xmlns:chats="using:Telegram.Controls.Chats"
                    xmlns:messages="using:Telegram.Controls.Messages"
                    xmlns:primitives="using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls.Primitives"
                    xmlns:xaml="using:Microsoft.Graphics.Canvas.UI.Xaml">

    <!--
        LINUX OVERRIDES - merged LAST in Telegram/App.xaml.

        Two dictionaries in this folder and they are not interchangeable:

          Hubs/LinuxResources.xaml  is merged FIRST, right after XamlControlsResources, and only
                                    carries keys that WinUI defines and Uno's Fluent theme does
                                    not, so that the dictionaries merged after it can be BasedOn
                                    them.
          Hubs/LinuxOverrides.xaml  (this one) is merged LAST, so it can be BasedOn anything the
                                    app defines and so that a key redefined here wins.

        A StaticResource in a merged dictionary only sees the dictionaries merged ahead of it, and
        one that resolves to nothing takes the whole application's resources down at startup - so
        anything with a BasedOn belongs here, not there.

        What goes in here: styles for controls whose only <Style TargetType> in Themes/ carries the
        win: prefix, i.e. is compiled on Windows and dropped on Skia. A control in that state has
        NO template at all, which does not throw and does not warn: it measures 0x0 and the button
        is simply not there.
    -->

    <!--
        MoreButton - the header overflow ("...") of the chat, the gallery, the forum topic pane and
        the chat list's multiple-selection bar. Its style (Themes/Generic.xaml, win:-only) is
        BasedOn DefaultGlyphButtonStyle and its template draws the icon with
        <muxc:AnimatedIcon Source="{TemplateBinding IconSource}"> and no FallbackIconSource, so
        dropping the win: prefix would not be enough either: AnimatedIcon draws nothing without a
        fallback and Telegram.Assets.Icons is inert in this port (Xaml/IconStubs.cs).

        DefaultGlyphButtonStyle (Common/CommonStyles.xaml) is not win:-prefixed, already carries
        the 48x48 that upstream restates through AppBarThemeCompactHeight, and paints its Glyph
        through a ContentPresenter. E10C is the same glyph the win: style declares, and it is in
        Assets/Fonts/Telegram.ttf (checked: the face covers e10a-e10c), which is what
        SymbolThemeFontFamily resolves to here.
    -->
    <Style TargetType="controls:MoreButton"
           BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultGlyphButtonStyle}">
        <Setter Property="Glyph"
                Value="&#xE10C;" />
        <Setter Property="AutomationProperties.Name"
                Value="{CustomResource AccDescrMoreOptions}" />
        <Setter Property="ToolTipService.ToolTip"
                Value="{CustomResource AccDescrMoreOptions}" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground"
                Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush"
                Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        IconBadgeButtonStyle - the rows of the settings root (Views/SettingsPage.xaml).

        Same defect as MoreButton, one layer down: the upstream template
        (Themes/BadgeButton_themeresources.xaml:740) draws the row icon with

            <muxc:AnimatedIcon x:Name="Icon" Source="{TemplateBinding IconSource}" ... />

        and no FallbackIconSource. Telegram.Assets.Icons is generated by LottieGen on Win2D, so
        here every one of those sources is inert (Xaml/IconStubs.cs: TryCreateAnimatedVisual
        returns null), and AnimatedIcon with a null visual and no fallback draws nothing. The 48 px
        first column stays empty while the text, the badge and the chevron are drawn as usual - the
        row reads as if its icon failed to load. Cosmetic, never a throw, which is why it survived
        this long.

        The fix is the one the CheckBox template already proves works here: a real glyph. Rather
        than nest a FontIconSource inside AnimatedIcon.FallbackIconSource, this template drops
        AnimatedIcon entirely and uses the very element the other three SettingsButton templates in
        BadgeButton_themeresources.xaml already use (:87, :355, :499):

            <TextBlock x:Name="GlyphPresenter" Text="{TemplateBinding Glyph}" ... />

        The name matters and is not decoration: SettingsButton.OnApplyTemplate looks up exactly
        "GlyphPresenter" and collapses it when ComputedIsGlyphVisible is false, i.e. when Glyph is
        empty (Controls/SettingsButton.cs:47 and :224). So a row that has no glyph keeps the
        upstream look instead of reserving an empty column, with no extra code.

        The glyphs themselves are set per row in Views/SettingsPage.xaml. Setting Glyph there is
        inert on Windows: the win: template above never reads it, and ComputedIsGlyphVisible only
        drives a GlyphPresenter that template does not have.

        Everything else here is upstream's template verbatim: the 48/* columns, RootGrid, the
        ContentPresenter and the BadgePresenter with its clip. The only other removal is the two
        <VisualState.Setters> that wrote Icon.(muxc:AnimatedIcon.State) on PointerOver/Pressed -
        there is no element named Icon any more, and a setter target that does not resolve is a
        parse-time failure of the whole dictionary.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="IconBadgeButtonStyle"
           TargetType="controls:SettingsButton">
        <Setter Property="Background"
                Value="Transparent" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush"
                Value="{ThemeResource TelegramSeparatorMediumBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness"
                Value="0" />
        <Setter Property="Padding"
                Value="12,0,0,0" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment"
                Value="Left" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment"
                Value="Stretch" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment"
                Value="Stretch" />
        <Setter Property="FontFamily"
                Value="{StaticResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight"
                Value="Normal" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize"
                Value="{ThemeResource ControlContentThemeFontSize}" />
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals"
                Value="True" />
        <Setter Property="Width"
                Value="Auto" />
        <Setter Property="Height"
                Value="Auto" />
        <Setter Property="MinHeight"
                Value="0" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="controls:SettingsButton">
                    <Grid Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPointerOver}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPressed}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Foreground"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="ContentPresenter">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource SystemControlForegroundBaseLowBrush}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="48" />
                            <ColumnDefinition />
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Border x:Name="RootGrid"
                                CornerRadius="4"
                                Margin="4,2"
                                Grid.ColumnSpan="2" />

                        <TextBlock x:Name="GlyphPresenter"
                                   Text="{TemplateBinding Glyph}"
                                   FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                   FontSize="20"
                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                   AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="ContentPresenter"
                                          FontFamily="{ThemeResource ContentControlThemeFontFamily}"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"
                                          BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                          BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                          ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                          ContentTransitions="{TemplateBinding ContentTransitions}"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                          Padding="0,9,12,10"
                                          VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                          Grid.Column="1" />
                        <ContentControl x:Name="BadgePresenter"
                                        FontFamily="{ThemeResource ContentControlThemeFontFamily}"
                                        Content="{TemplateBinding Badge}"
                                        Visibility="{TemplateBinding BadgeVisibility}"
                                        Foreground="{ThemeResource SystemControlDisabledChromeDisabledLowBrush}"
                                        Height="40"
                                        Padding="12,9,12,10"
                                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Right"
                                        IsTabStop="False"
                                        Grid.Column="1">
                            <ContentControl.ContentTransitions>
                                <TransitionCollection>
                                    <EntranceThemeTransition />
                                </TransitionCollection>
                            </ContentControl.ContentTransitions>
                            <ContentControl.Clip>
                                <RectangleGeometry Rect="0,0,3600,40" />
                            </ContentControl.Clip>
                        </ContentControl>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!--
        SettingsRadioButtonStyle - the three-way "Everybody / My contacts / Nobody" rows that ARE
        the privacy section. Thirteen pages ask for this key by name, 41 times in total
        (Style="{StaticResource SettingsRadioButtonStyle}").

        Both declarations in Themes/RadioButton_themeresources.xaml are win:-only: the implicit
        <win:Style TargetType="controls:SettingsRadioButton"> on line 12 and the keyed
        <win:Style x:Key="SettingsRadioButtonStyle"> on line 15. The implicit one is already
        covered - SettingsRadioButton's constructor sets DefaultStyleKey = typeof(RadioButton)
        under #if LINUX, so the control borrows Uno's RadioButton template. The KEYED one is not,
        and an unresolved {StaticResource} is not cosmetic here: it takes the whole application's
        resources down at startup, so the page never draws at all.

        Deliberately NO Template setter. An explicit Style sits above the built-in default style
        rather than replacing it, so leaving Template unset lets Uno's RadioButton template
        (reached through DefaultStyleKey above) still supply the ellipse, the check glyph and the
        content presenter. This style only restores what upstream's setters add around it:
        the settings-row background, the stretch, the padding and the 48 px minimum height.

        PrivacyRadioButton derives from SettingsRadioButton, so TargetType="controls:SettingsRadioButton"
        applies to both - which is exactly why the pages name the key explicitly instead of relying
        on an implicit style, since implicit styles are not inherited by derived types.

        What is lost against Windows: the DescriptionPresenter (a second line under the label) has
        no counterpart in Uno's template, so a SettingsRadioButton with Description set would drop
        that line. None of the thirteen privacy pages sets Description - they all use Content only.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="SettingsRadioButtonStyle"
           TargetType="controls:SettingsRadioButton">
        <Setter Property="Background"
                Value="{ThemeResource SettingsItemBackground}" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground"
                Value="{ThemeResource RadioButtonForeground}" />
        <Setter Property="Padding"
                Value="0,11,12,12" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment"
                Value="Stretch" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment"
                Value="Stretch" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment"
                Value="Left" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment"
                Value="Center" />
        <Setter Property="FontFamily"
                Value="{ThemeResource ContentControlThemeFontFamily}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize"
                Value="{ThemeResource ControlContentThemeFontSize}" />
        <Setter Property="MinHeight"
                Value="48" />
        <Setter Property="MinWidth"
                Value="120" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius"
                Value="0" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        ...and the IMPLICIT style for the same type, which the block above says was "already
        covered" and was not.

        Naming the key covers the thirteen privacy pages, because those name it too. It does not
        cover the pages that write plain <controls:SettingsRadioButton> and rely on upstream's
        implicit <win:Style TargetType="controls:SettingsRadioButton"> - which is dropped on Skia
        along with everything else win:. In this head those are Settings > Language (the 32 language
        rows, one SettingsRadioButton per row inside the ListView's ItemTemplate) and Settings >
        Data and storage (the "download folder" pair). They were coming out as bare Fluent radio
        buttons: no SettingsItemBackground, no 48 px row, none of the 0,11,12,12 padding, and not
        stretched to the width of the card, so the language list read as a stack of loose radio
        buttons instead of a settings list.

        BasedOn rather than a copy, so there stays ONE definition of what a settings radio row is;
        and no Template setter here either, for the reason the keyed style gives - an explicit style
        sits on top of the built-in default style rather than replacing it, so Uno's RadioButton
        template (reached through DefaultStyleKey = typeof(RadioButton) in the constructor) still
        supplies the ellipse, the check glyph and the content presenter.

        PrivacyRadioButton is NOT caught by this: an implicit style keys on the exact type, and it
        derives from SettingsRadioButton. That is deliberate and unchanged - it goes on naming the
        key, which is the same style.

        What is still lost against Windows is the DescriptionPresenter, and it is worth writing down
        why it is not being chased: (a) upstream declares it x:Load="False" and reaches it with
        GetTemplateChild, and PORTING.md section 6 has it measured that GetTemplateChild does not
        materialize an x:Load="False" element in Uno - the same trap the SettingsHeadline caption
        below had to be dug out of, so porting the template verbatim would not have brought the
        second line either; and (b) nothing in this codebase ever sets Description on a
        SettingsRadioButton. Every Description= in Views/ is on a SettingsButton, whose style in
        Themes/Generic.xaml is not win:-prefixed and whose DescriptionPresenter is deferred with
        x:DeferLoadStrategy="Lazy" precisely so it can be found. So the missing presenter is a
        divergence with no reachable caller; the missing implicit style was the visible half.
    -->
    <Style TargetType="controls:SettingsRadioButton"
           BasedOn="{StaticResource SettingsRadioButtonStyle}" />

    <!--
        SettingsHeadline - the animated illustration plus caption at the top of Blocked users
        (BlockedChats.tgs), Two-step verification (TwoFactorSetupIntro.tgs) and Auto-delete.

        Same shape as MoreButton: its only <Style TargetType="local:SettingsHeadline"> is
        win:-prefixed (Themes/Generic.xaml:2662) while the control sets
        DefaultStyleKey = typeof(SettingsHeadline) (Controls/SettingsHeadline.cs:20). A control
        whose default style key resolves to nothing gets no template: it measures 0x0, does not
        throw and does not warn, so the header simply is not there.

        This is upstream's template verbatim except for ONE change, and that change is required:
        the caption TextBlock carries x:Load="False" upstream and is materialized by
        GetTemplateChild("Headline") from OnApplyTemplate / OnTextChanged. PORTING.md 6 has it
        measured that GetTemplateChild does NOT materialize an x:Load="False" element in Uno, so
        keeping it would give the animation with no caption under it. Dropping x:Load costs
        nothing: TextBlockHelper.Markdown is bound to Text, which is empty when there is no
        caption, and an empty TextBlock draws nothing.

        AnimatedImage, TextBlockHelper and InfoBodyTextBlockStyle are all inside the subset.
    -->
    <Style TargetType="controls:SettingsHeadline">
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment"
                Value="Stretch" />
        <Setter Property="Padding"
                Value="0,16,0,16" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="controls:SettingsHeadline">
                    <Grid MaxWidth="1000"
                          Margin="24,0">
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <controls:AnimatedImage Source="{TemplateBinding Source}"
                                                LoopCount="{TemplateBinding LoopCount}"
                                                AutoPlay="True"
                                                IsCachingEnabled="False"
                                                DecodeFrameType="Logical"
                                                FrameSize="140,140"
                                                Width="140"
                                                Height="140"
                                                Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}" />
                        <TextBlock x:Name="Headline"
                                   common:TextBlockHelper.IsLink="{TemplateBinding IsLink}"
                                   common:TextBlockHelper.Markdown="{TemplateBinding Text}"
                                   Style="{StaticResource InfoBodyTextBlockStyle}"
                                   TextAlignment="Center"
                                   Margin="12,0,12,0"
                                   MaxWidth="480"
                                   Grid.Row="1" />
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!--
        LoopingPicker - the days / hours spinner of ChatMutePopup ("mute for...").

        Third case of the same shape (only <Style TargetType="local:LoopingPicker"> is win:-only,
        Themes/Generic.xaml:4174, and DefaultStyleKey = typeof(LoopingPicker)), but this one is NOT
        the harmless kind. MoreButton and SettingsHeadline merely measure 0x0 without a template;
        LoopingPicker.OnApplyTemplate (Controls/LoopingPicker.cs:36-47) dereferences three template
        parts with no null check at all:

            ValueText.Text = ...;  NextButton.Click += ...;  PrevButton.Click += ...;

        so a missing template is a NullReferenceException thrown out of the template pass, which
        takes the whole popup down rather than degrading the spinner - exactly what
        ScrollViewerScrim would have done.

        Upstream's template verbatim, with local: rewritten to controls:. Nothing in it needs
        anything outside the subset: GlyphButton, AnimatedTextBlock and the two theme brushes are
        all in, and the glyphs E0E4 / E0E5 are in Assets/Fonts/Telegram.ttf.
    -->
    <Style TargetType="controls:LoopingPicker">
        <Setter Property="IsTabStop"
                Value="True" />
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals"
                Value="False" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="controls:LoopingPicker">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="FocusStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Unfocused" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerFocused" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="Focused">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="FocusHighlight.Background"
                                                Value="{ThemeResource ControlAltFillColorTertiaryBrush}" />
                                        <Setter Target="ValueText.Foreground"
                                                Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}" />
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                        <controls:GlyphButton x:Name="NextButton"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              Glyph="&#xE0E4;"
                                              IsTabStop="False"
                                              AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"
                                              Width="40"
                                              Height="40" />

                        <Grid x:Name="FocusHighlight"
                              Background="Transparent"
                              MinWidth="72"
                              Height="72"
                              CornerRadius="2"
                              Padding="0,6"
                              Margin="0,4"
                              Control.IsTemplateFocusTarget="True">
                            <controls:AnimatedTextBlock x:Name="ValueText"
                                                        Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                                        Padding="0,12,0,20"
                                                        FontFamily="Segoe UI"
                                                        FontSize="40"
                                                        FontWeight="Bold"
                                                        TextAlignment="Center"
                                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                        HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                                <controls:AnimatedTextBlock.TextStyle>
                                    <Style TargetType="TextBlock">
                                        <Setter Property="FontFamily"
                                                Value="Segoe UI" />
                                        <Setter Property="FontSize"
                                                Value="40" />
                                        <Setter Property="FontWeight"
                                                Value="Bold" />
                                        <Setter Property="TextLineBounds"
                                                Value="Tight" />
                                        <Setter Property="TextAlignment"
                                                Value="Center" />
                                    </Style>
                                </controls:AnimatedTextBlock.TextStyle>
                            </controls:AnimatedTextBlock>

                            <TextBlock Text="{TemplateBinding Header}"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                                       TextLineBounds="Tight"
                                       TextAlignment="Center"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Grid>

                        <controls:GlyphButton x:Name="PrevButton"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              Glyph="&#xE0E5;"
                                              IsTabStop="False"
                                              AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"
                                              Width="40"
                                              Height="40" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>


    <!--
        ================================================================================
        u-016: the six controls whose ONLY <Style TargetType> is win:-gated, so on Skia
        they get no template at all - they measure 0x0 and simply are not there, with no
        exception and no log line. Found by u-015's read-only sweep
        (unigram-linux/review/WIN-ONLY-STYLES.md), mechanism in PORTING.md 6.

        ALL SIX ARE COPIED, none redirected to a base class's style, and that was measured
        rather than preferred. Redirecting was the cheaper option offered for A1, A5 and
        C1, but each of those three resolves parts from ITS OWN template that no base
        template declares:
            ChatStickerButton  -> Icon            (ChatStickerButton.cs:371)
            GlassToggleButton  -> CheckedPart     (GlassToggleButton.cs:37)
            ChatPill           -> Photo, Title    (ChatPill.cs:37-38)
        Redirecting leaves those null. None of the three throws - each is null-guarded -
        so the failure would have been silent: a sticker button with no icon, a call
        button with no checked state, a giveaway pill with no avatar and no name. Copying
        costs a few hundred lines of XAML and changes nothing about the look.
        ================================================================================
    -->

    <!--
        A1 - ChatStickerButton, the emoji/sticker/GIF button of the composer
        (ChatView.xaml:1404, unconditional). This is the regression u-003 left behind: the
        merge removed the Control stub, the real class kept DefaultStyleKey =
        typeof(ChatStickerButton), and its only style is win:-only - so the button that
        FALTA 1.4 finally made real went straight back to measuring 0 in the shipped drop.
        Copied verbatim from Themes/Generic.xaml:7242-7348.
    -->

    <Style TargetType="chats:ChatStickerButton">
        <Setter Property="Background"
                Value="Transparent" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground"
                Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush"
                Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness"
                Value="0" />
        <Setter Property="Padding"
                Value="0" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment"
                Value="Left" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment"
                Value="Center" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment"
                Value="Top" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment"
                Value="Center" />
        <Setter Property="FontFamily"
                Value="{StaticResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize"
                Value="{StaticResource GlyphLargeFontSize}" />
        <Setter Property="Height"
                Value="48" />
        <Setter Property="Width"
                Value="48" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight"
                Value="Normal" />
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals"
                Value="True" />
        <Setter Property="FocusVisualMargin"
                Value="-3" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius"
                Value="{StaticResource GlyphButtonCornerRadius}" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="chats:ChatStickerButton">
                    <Grid Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                          CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                          Margin="{StaticResource GlyphButtonPadding}">
                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPointerOver}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPressed}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="Checked" />
                                <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPointerOver">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPointerOver}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPressed">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetProperty="Background"
                                                                       Storyboard.TargetName="RootGrid">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0"
                                                                    Value="{ThemeResource NavigationViewItemBackgroundPressed}" />
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="CheckedDisabled" />
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                        <Grid x:Name="RootGrid">
                            <TextBlock x:Name="ContentPresenter1"
                                       Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                       VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                       AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
                            <TextBlock x:Name="ContentPresenter2"
                                       Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                       VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                       AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />

                            <Border x:Name="Icon"
                                    Width="24"
                                    Height="24"
                                    AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
                        </Grid>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!--
        A2 - EmojiSearchBox, the search field at the top of all four u-003 drawers
        (EmojiDrawer.xaml:86, StickerDrawer.xaml:39, AnimationDrawer.xaml:33,
        EffectDrawer.xaml:41). Its base is a bare Control, so there is no base style to
        redirect to: copying is the only option. From Generic.xaml:2197-2239.
    -->

    <Style TargetType="controls:EmojiSearchBox">
        <Setter Property="IsTabStop"
                Value="False" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="controls:EmojiSearchBox">
                    <Grid>
                        <TextBox x:Name="TextField"
                                 PlaceholderText="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderText}"
                                 Style="{StaticResource NoDeleteTextBoxStyle}"
                                 Background="{ThemeResource TextControlBackgroundPointerOver}"
                                 BorderBrush="{ThemeResource ControlStrokeColorDefaultBrush}"
                                 Padding="36,5,6,6" />

                        <controls:AnimatedGlyphToggleButton x:Name="SearchButton"
                                                         Grid.Row="1"
